<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keiko Fujimori</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1975">1975</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keiko Fujimori is a Peruvian politician, the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberto-fujimori">Alberto Fujimori</a>, who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>'s first lady in the 1990s after her parents separated. As leader of the right-wing Popular Force party she was narrowly defeated in the presidential run-offs of 2011, 2016 and 2021, while her party dominated Congress after 2016. She was investigated over illegal campaign financing and spent periods in pre-trial detention. At her fourth attempt she narrowly won the run-off of June 2026 and became president in July 2026.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keiko-fujimori.jpg" alt="Keiko Fujimori" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministerio de la Producción · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pdta._Keiko_Fujimori_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
